First-read workflow for CA-HeteroLBM-Algorithm
==============================================

This file explains what a new user should read first after downloading this repository.


1. Start with the main overview
-------------------------------

Read:

  README.md

This file explains what CA-HeteroLBM is, what execution modes it supports, and shows quick build and run examples.


2. Understand the execution modes
---------------------------------

Read:

  docs/modes.txt

This file explains the supported execution modes:

  single-gpu
  multi-gpu
  optimized heterogeneous CPU+GPU
  GPU-aware optimized heterogeneous CPU+GPU


3. Learn how to build and run the solver
----------------------------------------

Read:

  docs/run_instructions.txt

This is the main practical instruction file. It explains:

  how to build the solver
  how to run single-GPU mode
  how to run multi-GPU mode
  how to run optimized heterogeneous mode
  how to run GPU-aware optimized heterogeneous mode
  how to run energy measurements
  how to run with or without the AdceWatt power meter


4. Understand the folder structure
----------------------------------

Read:

  docs/folder_details.md

This file explains what each folder contains, including:

  src/
  bin/
  input/
  cudafunc/
  3dbase/
  3dgeneral/
  3dsetup/
  results_summary/


5. Build and run on another machine
-----------------------------------

Read:

  docs/build_and_run_on_another_system.txt

This file is useful when the solver is moved to a different server or HPC system. The tuned heterogeneous profiles are platform-specific, so another machine may require retuning of the CPU Z-plane count and OpenMP thread count.


6. Energy measurement details
-----------------------------

Read:

  docs/energy_measurement_notes.txt

This file is useful only if the user wants to reproduce the AdceWatt energy measurement workflow. Users without the AdceWatt power meter can still run all solver modes with:

  bin/run_lbm_baseline.py


7. Main code files
------------------

To understand the code flow, read these files:

  src/main_plane_couette_3D_CUDA_paramcalc_virtual_nodes_mpi_omp_cuda_1dZsv3.cu
  bin/run_lbm_baseline.py
  bin/run_lbm_energy_adcewatt.py

The CUDA/MPI/OpenMP solver logic is in the source file. The baseline runner launches normal timing and correctness runs. The energy runner launches runs with AdceWatt energy measurement.


Recommended reading order
-------------------------

For most users, the recommended order is:

  1. README.md
  2. docs/modes.txt
  3. docs/run_instructions.txt
  4. docs/folder_details.md

For users who want energy measurements, also read:

  docs/energy_measurement_notes.txt

For users moving the code to another machine, also read:

  docs/build_and_run_on_another_system.txt
  
  
  
  
  
  
